		(property "Notes" "Battery-side bulk (C432/C532): Panasonic ZA hybrid polymer (conductive polymer + liquid electrolyte). 100 uF with no DC-bias loss, 30 mOhm and 2 A at 100 kHz like the solid polymer it replaced, but leakage <= 0.01CV = 25 uA max (the JIERR solid polymer was 0.2CV = 500 uA). It is the only bulk cap biased in idle (from PACK_P whenever the gauge FETs are on), so its leakage is idle drain. 10,000 h at 105 C. MLCCs C431/C434/C435 carry the HF ripple"
			(at 193.05 110.7 0)
